{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Provide a working IMAP service on node1 for the archive account using a dedicated demonstration password.","status":"satisfied","summary":"An AlmaLinux-compatible Dovecot package was installed and configured for the archive Maildir. The service was enabled, active, listening on IMAPS port 993, and authenticated the archive account with a newly generated dedicated credential. It remained operational after node1 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5e4422155f094261","cmd-10ecc731c99c4f75","cmd-99660f31ceca4183","cmd-0b52ed3e136d4fae"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"Allow node2 to authenticate and retrieve both messages while preserving Message-ID values, bodies, and the read/unread state specified in mailbox.tsv.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct IMAPS tests from node2 authenticated successfully and retrieved exactly two messages. one.eml retained Message-ID <one@branch.test>, body “Shipment arrived.”, and the \\Seen flag; two.eml retained Message-ID <two@branch.test>, body “Shipment departed.”, and lacked \\Seen. The same result was observed after both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7d9b516975064ddb","cmd-b7e901b3af5c4515","cmd-c9effac972bd4069","cmd-4dc2321a4f4c4d2d","cmd-3e723575950a41c2"]},{"id":"req-3","requirement":"Keep the supplied staged mailbox under /srv/legacy2/imap-maildir-cutover intact because it is the source copy.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All three staged files had the same SHA-256 values before and after the implementation and after node1 restarted. The operational Maildir contains separately copied messages whose hashes match the staged originals.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-b7e901b3af5c4515","cmd-10ecc731c99c4f75","cmd-99660f31ceca4183","cmd-0b52ed3e136d4fae"]},{"id":"req-4","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on AlmaLinux 9.6 with kernel 5.14.0-570.12.1.el9_6.x86_64. Dovecot was installed from the EL9 AppStream repository, ran successfully, and recovered after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7d9b516975064ddb","cmd-390c251a152a41a1","cmd-5e4422155f094261","cmd-0b52ed3e136d4fae","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.88,"summary":"The implementation mutations—package installation, archive account and Maildir creation, TLS/configuration, firewall rule, service enablement, and required restarts—were causally related to the task or mandatory restart evidence. No failed-service, package-health, or temporary-file residue was observed. The unnecessary retained mutations were the root authorized-key addition on node1 and the root private key/known-hosts files on node2: they supported bounded remote evidence collection, but no cleanup was shown, leaving persistent inter-node root SSH access after verification. The initially failed IMAP parsing attempt did not establish an additional managed-state mutation and was corrected immediately.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5e4422155f094261","cmd-10ecc731c99c4f75","cmd-959968a2bb5548d2","cmd-75480d57f8624a10","cmd-c9effac972bd4069","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct end-to-end evidence. Node2 successfully authenticated to node1 and retrieved both preserved messages, the staged source hashes remained unchanged, and the OS/kernel were retained. The provider-wide restart protocol was also completed coherently on both nodes: healthy pre-restart states and acknowledgements were captured, boot identities changed, fixed lifecycle observations independently confirmed those changes, and service/network/data behavior recovered afterward.","limitations":["The final integrity check revalidated staged-file contents by SHA-256 but did not repeat the complete permissions, ownership, mtime, and directory-structure inventory from the preparation baseline.","The IMAPS client disabled certificate validation and hostname checking because the service used a self-signed certificate. This does not contradict the stated contract, but it does not demonstrate trusted server identity validation.","Persistent root SSH key artifacts used for verification were not shown as removed."]}
